          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.133,
          "end": 46.466,
          "en": "with all these components, which we are building,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.466,
          "end": 49.3,
          "en": "in the end we're just splitting up our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.3,
          "end": 52.866,
          "en": "across multiple files and building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.866,
          "end": 53.133,
          "en": "across multiple files and building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.133,
          "end": 56.533,
          "en": "so that if we want to have more than one expense item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.533,
          "end": 59.966,
          "en": "we can just use our custom ExpenseItem component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.966,
          "end": 61.7,
          "en": "multiple times instead of repeating all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.7,
          "end": 63.2,
          "en": "multiple times instead of repeating all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.2,
          "end": 66.2,
          "en": "that code multiple times, that's the idea behind components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.2,
          "end": 68.866,
          "en": "that code multiple times, that's the idea behind components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.866,
          "end": 72.43299999999999,
          "en": "In the end, what ends up on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
